source: tests/golden/harness.rs
---
  x `core/early` expands FLAVOUR above the flavour gate
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-fragment/image.kdl:15:9]
 14 |     core {
 15 |         early
    :         ^^|^^
    :           `-- listed above the first flavour-gated component
 16 |     }
    `----
  help: ARG FLAVOUR is declared directly above the first gated entry, so a
        fragment before it would expand to an empty string

  x `core/silent` is listed under `dev` but its fragment sets no FLAVOUR_GATE
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-fragment/image.kdl:20:13]
 19 |         core {
 20 |             silent
    :             ^^^|^^
    :                `-- the flavour gate would be silently ignored
 21 |         }
    `----
  help: a fragment is emitted unconditionally, so anything it runs has to
        carry the gate itself

  x `core/mismatched` is listed under `dev` but its fragment gates on `server`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-fragment/image.kdl:23:13]
 22 |         core {
 23 |             mismatched
    :             ^^^^^|^^^^
    :                  `-- listed here
 24 |         }
    `----
